  - Coupling was not in the `RebuildWater` mesh generator itself (it already latched one water level and projects all water corners with that same value via `_projectPosition(worldX, worldY, wl)` in [HeightFieldRenderer.cs line ~1236](E:/Dev/WorldSphereMod/External/Compound-Spheres/CompoundSpheres/HeightFieldRenderer.cs#L1236-1277).
  - The problematic path was the `sampleWaterLevel` input chain in [Core.cs around `ConfigureHeightField`](E:/Dev/WorldSphereMod/WorldSphereMod/Code/Core.cs#L1490-L1503); it is now pinned to `seaLevel` with an explicit 1-line comment, so seabed can only affect depth-color, not surface Y.
- Programmatic measurement from `/diag/water_samples` (live):
  - Deep water tile: `(tx,ty)=(32,32)` — `tileY=0.003983`, `seabedY=0.003983`, `waterY=2.000000`
  - Shallow water tile: `(tx,ty)=(192,192)` — `tileY=0.868746`, `seabedY=0.868746`, `waterY=2.000000`
  - PASS: `|waterY_deep - waterY_shallow| = 0.000000` (flat; same sea-level plane)
- Next blocker: none


